  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The short answer",
      "items": [
        "The Lab's API key lives only in surface B",
        "the gateway's signing key only behind its DID log, which poly pins",
        "On poly's side the only keys are its own: the ledger signer and a person's approval key, both planned for the box and neither present yet"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Not shown here",
      "items": [
        "The agent, the proxy and the tunnel, which carry requests but hold no key the demo depends on",
        "the channel, the Desk and the policy, drawn by the run-time questions",
        "Connected but out of scope: OAuth discovery proxy, 2Dee tunnel, Agent Lab host, gateway channel, Desk machine, Desk policy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "What it guarantees",
      "items": [
        "poly holds no key of the Lab. The MCP client refuses a configuration that carries a credential under any header name, and PL6825 finds none in the files the certificate binds: The key stays in the gateway, as the Hello, Gateway recipe teaches.",
        "An email change runs only after a person signs its approval; a phone or address change runs at once."
      ]
    }
  ]
